name: sim.floatingViewAdd
description: Adds a floating view to current page
luaSynopsis: int floatingViewHandle = sim.floatingViewAdd(float posX, float posY, float sizeX, float sizeY, int options)
pythonSynopsis: int floatingViewHandle = sim.floatingViewAdd(float posX, float posY, float sizeX, float sizeY, int options)
inputs:
1. posX & posY: relative position of the center of the floating view. Accepted values are between 0.0 and 1.0
2. sizeX & sizeY: relative size of the floating view. Accepted values are between 0.0 and 1.0
3. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): double click allows swapping the floating view with the main view
    - bit1 set (2): the floating view doesn't have a close button
    - bit2 set (4): the floating view cannot be shifted
    - bit3 set (8): the floating view cannot be resized
outputs:
1. floatingViewHandle: handle of the floating view
